-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SCOPE — THIS NOTICE DOES NOT GRANT RIGHTS OVER THE SOURCE TEXTS.

The reservation above covers Al Marfa Technologies' own work. It confers no
rights over, and does not extend to, the Qur'anic text, the translations, or the
fonts this pipeline compiles. Those belong to their respective rights holders and
carry their own, mostly narrower terms — several are non-commercial,
attribution-required and verbatim-only, and one (Junagarhi) is public domain and
therefore cannot be claimed by anyone, including us.

ATTRIBUTION.md is canonical for what may be redistributed and under what
obligations; config/sources.yaml records the terms per resource (the `license`
field, which is compiled into the database and its published edition artifacts).

EXCEPTION TO THE SCOPE LIMIT — ORIGINAL DIGITAL RECONSTRUCTIONS.

The scope limit above excludes source *texts*: the words of a translation or
the Qur'anic Arabic. It does not exclude original digital renderings this
project produces from those texts where no equivalent digital rendering
existed before. Two such works are asserted as Al Marfa Technologies' own
protectable expression, reservation and all: the OCR-reconstructed, nukta-
restored Ahsanul Kalam Hindi text compiled by this pipeline (ATTRIBUTION.md
§4), and any Roman Urdu / Devanagari transliteration text produced by the
sibling `alquran-roman-urdu` project once it ships here. Scraping, bulk
extraction, or reuse of those specific compiled texts requires the owner's
prior written permission, same as the pipeline code — this does not touch the
public-domain or separately-licensed status of the underlying source
translations themselves.
